return services specific to that namespace. But since the tool's parameters don't include a namespace, maybe it's designed to work within that context. Alternatively, maybe I need to use the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd to get the services in the namespace. For example, running 'kubectl get services -n astronomy-shop'. \n\nBut the user's first step was to use get_services. Maybe the Grafana instance is already set up to show services in that namespace. However, if the tool doesn't take a namespace parameter, it might not be accurate. But since the user instructed to start with get_services, I should proceed with that. \n\nSo the tool call would be to get_services with no arguments. The response would give a list of services. Then, based on that list, I can proceed to check each service's health, metrics, dependencies, etc. \n\nAlternatively, if the get_services tool isn't scoped to the namespace, the list might include services from other namespaces, which would complicate things. But given the user's setup, perhaps the Grafana instance is already configured for the astronomy-shop namespace. \n\nIn any case, the first step is to get the list of services. So the correct tool call is get_services with no arguments. Then, once I have the services, I can move on to checking their metrics, traces, and dependencies.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{}', 'name': 'get_services'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-98ae6dd5cd0cb1d3', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 579, 'prompt_tokens': 2473, 'total_tokens': 3052, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc38-c578-7f91-9d7d-f3d3c5ac7691-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_services', 'args': {}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-98ae6dd5cd0cb1d3